    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0512" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/1572</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-07-10"><hi rendition="#italic">July 10,
                        1923</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received July 18.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 188</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    Committee composed of the Minister of Finance, the Financial Adviser and the
                    General Receiver of Customs, has completed its work on the internal revenue law.
                    A copy of the proposed draft of law has been furnished me by the Financial
                    Adviser and is now being carefully considered by this Office. It is not my
                    intention to present this draft of law <pb facs="0513" n="389" xml:id="pg389"/>
                    to the Haitian Government until an agreement between the two governments has
                    been effected forming the basis for the law.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John H. Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
